implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of this task's own diff (the three files), then complete_task with the step-4 evidence. If the review changes any file, re-run step 4 and submit that fresh output.
- Parity: re-read MoeMessageDispatcher.kt lines 110-142 and MoeNotificationService.kt.
  - Every title, message and kind matches char-for-char, and DONE has no button.
  - Nothing notifies for STATE_SNAPSHOT, TASK_DELETED, a same-status frame, BACKLOG/PLANNING/WORKING/ARCHIVED, or a frame before the first snapshot.
  - The '](' -> '] (' rewrite is the ONLY intentional divergence, and it carries its comment.
- Twice or concurrently:
  - a burst of frames is decided frame by frame from the cache;
  - activate() registers exactly once;
  - a View Task click after dispose or deactivate lands in the error handling path, not an unhandled rejection.
- Null, empty or huge input: an undefined or empty title, a newline in a title, an unknown status (no notice). 50 DONE frames give 50 notices, the same as JetBrains (accepted).
- Mutation spot-check in the step-4 snapshot dir $S (outside the checkout, never in it). Each of these must turn `node --test tests/task-notifier.test.cjs` red; restore by re-copying:
  - delete the same-status guard;
  - return a no-op Disposable;
  - drop the '](' rewrite;
  - drop the rejection handler.
- Scope: complete_step.modifiedFiles lists exactly moe-vscode/src/util/TaskNotifier.ts, moe-vscode/src/extension.ts and moe-vscode/tests/task-notifier.test.cjs (DoD 4). Peer rows may hold dirty edits in MoeDaemonClient.ts or package.json. Leave them alone and never stage them.
